<title>USA: Tennessee Gas Pipeline may issue $800 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Tennessee Gas Pipeline may issue $800 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tennessee Gas Pipeline is expected to tap the corporate bond primary market with a $800 million three-part debt offering this week, market sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The deal is expcted to consist of a 20-year debt issue, a 30-year with a 10-year put option, and a 40-year tranche, sources said.</p>
<p>The offering, which is rated Baa3/BBB, will be underwritten by lead manager Donaldson Lufkin &amp; Jenrette Securities, sources added.</p>
<p>(( --Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
